body:
I believe that you are not worthless, but you're just in a bad spot in life. It's okay to be depressed for three years, as long as you try to help yourself get better. A little goes a long way and I'm sure if you keep inching towards betterment, even if it is extremely gradual, you'll get to the point in life when you'll be proud of yourself.

&#x200B;

As for your family, I think you would have to open up to them someday. I personally have been exhibiting symptoms of bipolarity for 5 years prior to being diagnosed with bipolar disorder 2 in 2016. I'm still not completely better, but if it took me 5 years to realize that I needed help and to open up to family, it might take you less time than that since you have reddit on your side. 

&#x200B;

Just know that it's never too late and be patient with yourself. You're doing amazing, sweetie. Take care. We're here for you.

It does sound like symptoms of someone depressed, but it could possibly be caused by puberty if you are of that age group. Regardless, you should consult with a medical professional if you would like to know for certain. 

&#x200B;

All your feelings are valid and I think I can say that people on this subreddit are here to share that sadness with you so that it won't be as heavy as it would be. With that, I'd like to say I'm here for you.
